33	/// Type of first argument of 'execute' function overload defines what INPUT DataType it is used for.
34	/// Return type defines what is the OUTPUT (return) type of the CH function.
35	/// Corresponding types:
36	///  - UInt16     => DataTypeDate
37	///  - UInt32     => DataTypeDateTime
38	///  - DateTime64 => DataTypeDateTime64
39	/// Please note that INPUT and OUTPUT types may differ, e.g.:
40	///  - 'AddSecondsImpl::execute(UInt32, ...) -> UInt32' is available to the ClickHouse users as 'addSeconds(DateTime, ...) -> DateTime'
41	///  - 'AddSecondsImpl::execute(UInt16, ...) -> UInt32' is available to the ClickHouse users as 'addSeconds(Date, ...) -> DateTime'
